title: Social welfare policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: social_welfare_timer = 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: labor_minister_party = "PPS" and pps_in_government = 1 and social_welfare_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/ZiemięckiBronisław.jpg
#Social welfare programs

= Social Welfare Policy

With the Labor and Social Welfare ministry, we can increase social welfare spending as part of our social democratic reformist_dissent

- @reduce_spending: Reduce spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending: Increase spending on welfare.
- @increase_spending_unemployed: Increase spending (welfare levels will remain about the same).
- @spending_same: Keep spending the same.
- @spending_same_unemployed: Keep spending the same (effectively a service cut).
- @easy_discard
#- @cancel_advisor_action

@reduce_spending
subtitle: This will hurt our proletarian base. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; workers_pps -= 8; unemployed_spd -= 8; workers_kpp += 5; welfare -= 1; nationalisy_dissent += 10; internationalist_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; dvp_relation += 5; z_relation += 3; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have reduced levels of social welfare spending. This means more poverty and suffering for the working class. Our detractors claim that we are sacrificing proletarian livelihoods for the sake of class peace with the bourgeoisie. Are they wrong? Are the workers wrong to turn to the Communists, in light of our choices?


@increase_spending
view-if: unemployed <= 15
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

We have increased welfare spending. Our proletarian base is pleased.

[? if psl_w_in_government or psl_p_in_government : Our coalition partners express their concern over increased spending on social welfare, emphasizing the need for fiscal conservatism. ?]

@increase_spending_unemployed
view-if: unemployed > 15
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 0; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid to maintain the same benefits. -1 Budget

Increasing welfare spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we are essentially treading water.

@spending_same
view-if: unemployed <= 15

We have kept welfare spending the same.


@spending_same_unemployed
view-if: unemployed > 15
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 4; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 8 if in_popular_front or in_left_front
subtitle: The increased levels of unemployment necessitate more spending on aid.

Increasing welfare spending is necessary in light of the rise in unemployment, so we have essentially cut welfare. The workers are justifiably displeased - we are sacrificing their livelihoods to appease bourgeois demands for austerity.

[? if in_popular_front or in_left_front: The KPD is turning against us for our welfare policy. ?]
